 "description": "Food-derived medium: metabolizable components of Mammee apple (Mammea americana) [Fruits] from FooDB, plus a standard M9 mineral base. Organic components use presence-based uptake bounds; FooDB content retained. Measured compounds with no BiGG exchange are listed under uncovered.",
 "namespace": "bigg",
 "provenance": {
  "source_type": "database",
  "citation": "FooDB v2020-04-07 (Wishart DS et al., foodb.ca). Content sources: DUKE, USDA.",
  "doi": "",
  "url": "https://foodb.ca/downloads",
  "notes": "Organic components mapped from FooDB compounds to BiGG via InChIKey/name. Mineral base added. Bounds presence-based; foodb_content retained. Unmapped measured compounds kept in uncovered (v2 completeness fix). IMPORTANT: composition values are taken from the archived FooDB 2020-04-07 CSV data release; FooDB's live food page no longer displays this bulk composition, so it will appear empty. Verify individual compounds via the per-component cross-reference links. Underlying content was aggregated by FooDB from USDA / DTU / Phenol Explorer.",
  "data_release": "FooDB 2020-04-07 CSV release (foodb.ca/downloads)",
  "food_record": "https://foodb.ca/foods/FOOD00405",
  "verification": "expert-curated (multi-source food composition; growth-relevant profile completed, FooDB noise removed)",
  "curation_date": "2026-07-17",
  "curation_sources": [
   "USDA SR 'Mammy-apple (mamey), raw' NDB 09131 (nutrient panel per en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mammea_americana)",
   "da Silva et al. 2020, 'Metabolite Profiling by UPLC-MSE, NMR... Mamey Apple', PMC7024372 (sugars & organic acids by NMR)",
   "Cardona-Marin et al. 2021, 'Nutritional characteristics and phenolic compounds of ripe fruit pulp from six accessions of Mammea americana L.', IJASFT 8:242 (agriscigroup.us) — proximates & phenolics",
   "PMC11013721 — mamey pulp cell-wall / pectin characterisation",
   "FooDB FOOD00405"
  ],
  "curation_notes": "Dominant carbon/energy source is the soluble-sugar + pectin fraction of the 12.5 g/100g carbohydrate; free sugars rank sucrose>fructose>glucose (NMR). Mamey is a mild, LOW-acid fruit (ash 0.18 g), organic acids modest with citric predominant (citric>malic>tartaric); citrate/malate present but not individually quantified in the literature. NMR free-sugar amounts are lower bounds (NMR under-captures total soluble sugar). Confidence medium because per-100g absolute sugar and organic-acid values are",
  "curation_added": [
   "individual free sugars (sucrose>fructose>glucose) with NMR-based amounts",
   "shikimic acid",
   "formic acid",
   "citric acid (predominant organic acid, qualitative)",
   "malic acid",
   "proximates: water, total carbohydrate, dietary fibre/pectin, protein, fat",
   "consolidated single 'iron' value"
  ],
  "curation_removed": [
